#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# echo_evaluation

#% text
# `echo_evaluation(e)` prints `e` before it is evaluated, then its value, and gives the value; `echo_evaluation(e, label)` prints both after the label, `echo_evaluation(e, before -> after)` after their own labels, and `echo_evaluation(e, label, f)` prints `f` of the value.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The argument is held; constructors such as `add` have already folded numbers when it is printed.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
echo_evaluation(2^3)
#% output
#| quote(2^3)
#| 8
#= 8

#% cell
echo_evaluation(reverse(range(4)), "input:" -> "result:")
#% output
#| input: quote(reverse(range(4)))
#| result: [4, 3, 2, 1]
#= [4, 3, 2, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `echo`, `print`, `echo_label`
